<title>GERMANY: German airports details Jan-Sept cargo traffic.</title>
<headline>German airports details Jan-Sept cargo traffic.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows total,flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports January-September 1996 with percentage changes from a year ago, as published by the German airports association (ADV).</p>
<p>    AIRPORT	     FLOWN   TRUCKED  TOTAL    % CHANGE</p>
<p>    Berlin (total)    23,159   4,480   27,639    +9.9</p>
<p>    - Tegel	     13,777   4,235   18,012   +12.1</p>
<p>    - Tempelhof	    258	 0	258   -53.1</p>
<p>    - Schoenefeld	9,124     245    9,369    +9.6</p>
<p>    Bremen		 1,918  17,776   19,694   +17.3</p>
<p>    Dresden		1,058   2,013    3,071   +19.7</p>
<p>    Duessseldorf	41,460     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>    Frankfurt	  995,318     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>    Hamburg	     27,153     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>    Hannover	     7,923     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>    Cologne	    232,231  23,003  255,234     +8.9</p>
<p>    Leipzig/Halle	2,244   1,060    3,304    +54.1</p>
<p>    Munich		58,053     n/a	n/a</p>
<p>    Muenster/Osnabrueck  506   9,228    9,734    +12.3</p>
<p>    Nuremberg	   32,897     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>    Saarbruecken	   676   1,177    1,853     -7.0</p>
<p>    Stuttgart	   13,746  39,946   53,692     +3.5</p>
<p>    TOTAL	    1,438,342     n/a     n/a</p>
<p>Notes: No overall air cargo total is given because several large airports with known large trucking volumes including Frankfurt, Munich and Duesseldorf do not release trucking figures. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
